From: timmyspurs12 <196032606+timmyspurs12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 14:27:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Daily posting audit: owner-fenced claims, TTL derivation,
 override warning, bounded reconciliation
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Source-level audit of dailyPost.ts per review — NEW commit (6852e00 unamended):

1. Claim-owner fencing: every execution carries a unique owner token stored
   in the claim. ALL claim writes (pre-submit->submitting transition,
   completion ->done, adoption, TTL renewal, stale release, moderator
   override clear) run as WATCH/MULTI/EXEC transactions that re-verify the
   observed owner token + phase before writing. Mechanism confirmed against
   installed typings (RedisClient.watch(...keys) -> TxClientLike with
   multi/set{expiration}/del/expire/exec/unwatch; plain-client read between
   watch and multi per the store-verified pattern). A fenced loser never
   overwrites, never releases, never submits — it re-reads and responds to
   the current state. Tests: A-claims-pauses/B-reclaims/A-resumes race
   (A submits nothing; B's claim intact), submitting-transition fence abort,
   and stale-release fence abort.

2. TTL review: routes derive the UTC day from the server clock (code-verified
   in scheduler.ts/menu.ts/triggers.ts), so delayed redelivery or late
   moderator action cannot target a past day. Day D's claim is targetable at
   most ~24h (+00:05 cron offset; >5min skew required to straddle midnight);
   the 48h claim TTL strictly exceeds that window — expiry can never precede
   the last targeting, so it cannot produce a duplicate. Derivation documented
   in code + runbook; uncertain claims re-arm TTL on every encounter.

3. Override semantics: the menu's FIRST-click confirmation text now carries
   the explicit duplicate warning ('if the original request was accepted
   later, the replacement CAN duplicate it') BEFORE the second click; the
   success toast repeats it; README and runbook document the same.

4. Reconciliation bounds: confirmed ListingFetchOptions {limit, pageSize} —
   getNewPosts returns at most the newest 50. 'No match' in a limited window
   is never proof of non-existence; it always yields uncertain, never a
   recreation. Test added: truncated listing with the matching post beyond
   the limit -> uncertain, no recreate.

Battery: lint 0, tsc 0, build OK, spec 18/18, unit 73/73 (25 daily-post
tests), harness 8/8, audit:bundle OK (34 answers). Diff scoped to
dailyPost.ts, its tests, menu.ts override text, and docs. Local only —
NOT pushed.

